nning."]}, "overview": "Cory Booker seeks another term in a state that leans Democratic in federal races, and every major race rating places this contest in the safest Democratic category. Booker enters October with roughly $22.6 million on hand after raising more than $20 million; Justin Murphy has raised about $63,000 and had under $10,000 in the bank in mid-October, with no outside spending reported on either side. Prediction markets put Democratic odds near 97 percent or higher.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on the state's lean, the midterm environment, incumbency and the money gap. The candidates debated several times in October, and Murphy earned praise from Republicans for his performances, but no evidence has emerged of a competitive race. Booker's late campaigning for a Democrat in Mississippi further suggests his own seat is not a concern.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 16.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9897, "margin": 16.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9901, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.991, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9894, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9935, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9868, "margin": 16.6}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9884, "margin": 17.0},